-- title:
--   The deleted tail of a bounded matrix function is bounded
-- statement:
--   Sign matrices are Boolean $m\times m$ matrices; $\mathrm{row}(\sigma)$ is the matrix with entries $\sigma_i$ in row $i$, $S_i$ denotes row $i$ of $S$, and $\oplus$ is entrywise XOR. For a function $f$ on sign matrices let $C_{k,l}(f)=\sum_{|s|=k,|t|=l}\hat f(s\times t)$ be the sum of Fourier coefficients over $k\times l$ rectangles. Let $|f|\le M$, $d\ge4$ with $m\le2^{d-2}$, and $|s|,|u|\le1$. Then the deleted tail satisfies
--   $$
--   \Bigl|\sum_{k>d,\ l>d}C_{k,l}(f)\,s^ku^l\,2^{-kl}\Bigr|\le M .
--   $$
--
--   The damping factor $2^{-kl}$ beats the number of large rectangles.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/Cotype/DeletedTail.lean#L89-L134

